# The only environment variable this app reads. Copy to `.env.local` (or
# `.env`) — never commit the copy; `.env*` is gitignored and only this
# `.example` is tracked.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is the origin of the Identity Worker — the BFF for this
# app. There is no separate backend service: the Worker serves both the API
# routes and the built `dist/` of this app, and the two ship as one release
# unit. Pointing this at anything other than a Worker origin would break that.
#
# The value must be an absolute origin, not a relative path. The dev server and
# the deployed app are on different origins, and a relative URL would resolve
# against whichever one happened to load the bundle.
#
# For local `wrangler dev` against the Worker, use the origin `wrangler dev`
# prints (by default http://localhost:8787). Every route on it except `/health`
# and `/ready` answers 501 in the bootstrap phase, and this UI renders that
# honestly rather than pretending otherwise.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
